-- title:
--   Hecke equivariance of an abelian-quotient family at p
-- statement:
--   Fix $N_0 \ge 1$ and a prime $p$ with $p \nmid N_0$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$, a level datum $\Lambda$ for $(N_0,p,A)$ — consisting of a morphism $\sigma_A \colon \operatorname{Spec} A \to \operatorname{Spec}$ of the localisation of $\mathbb Q$ at $p$ lifting the generic point, a scheme $X$ over that base with a relative group law, and bijections $\Lambda.\mathrm{pts}$ from $J_0(N_0)(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ onto the generic points of $X$ and $\Lambda.\mathrm{ptsSp}$ from $J_0(N_0)$ over the residue field of $A$ onto the points over $\operatorname{res}_A \circ \sigma_A$ — satisfying `IsJacobian`, and a Néron object $O$ at level $N_0p$ over $\Lambda$. Let $\mathrm{abq}$ be a family, indexed by the $m$ coprime to $p$, of additive maps $O.\mathrm{finPts}\,m \to J_0(N_0)(\overline{\mathbb Q})^2$, where $O.\mathrm{finPts}\,m$ is the subgroup generated by the $m$-torsion points of $J_0(N_0p)(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ whose associated generic point of $O.G$ factors through an $A$-point. Assume: each value is $m$-torsion; for every $x$ and every $A$-point $s$ over $\sigma_A$ whose restriction along $\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb Q} \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ is the point of $x$, the reduction mod the maximal ideal of $A$ of the $i$-th component of $\mathrm{abq}_m(x)$ is $\Lambda.\mathrm{ptsSp}^{-1}$ of the image of $s$ restricted to the residue field under $O.\mathrm{abqFibre}\,i$, for $i = 0,1$; the kernel of $\mathrm{abq}_m$ is $O.\mathrm{toricPts}\,m$; the image of $\mathrm{abq}_m$ is the full $m$-torsion of $J_0(N_0)(\overline{\mathbb Q})^2$; and $\mathrm{abq}_{m'}$ restricts to $\mathrm{abq}_m$ whenever $m \mid m'$. Then for $m$ coprime to $p$, a prime $\ell \nmid N_0p$ and $x \in O.\mathrm{finPts}\,m$ with $T_\ell x \in O.\mathrm{finPts}\,m$ (the action of the Hecke generator `heckeGen ℓ` in the algebra $\mathbb Z[T_\ell : \ell]$ via `heckeModuleBar`), one has $\mathrm{abq}_m(T_\ell x) = (T_\ell, T_\ell)\cdot \mathrm{abq}_m(x)$, the action on the target being that of `heckeModuleBar` at level $N_0$ in each coordinate.
--
--   This is the Hecke-equivariance property of the character-group/abelian-quotient description of the $m$-torsion of the Néron model of $J_0(N_0p)$ at $p$, in the form used in Ribet's level-lowering argument: any family of maps satisfying the reduction formula, the toric kernel, surjectivity and the divisibility compatibility is automatically equivariant for the Hecke operators away from $N_0p$. It is used in the construction of such a family, [`ModularCurve.JZeroNeronObjectAtP.exists_abq_family_of_coprime`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZeroNeronObjectAtP.exists_abq_family_of_coprime).
